# FINCH — testing

Coverage of 100% is not the goal. Coverage of critical correctness is (README §73).

## Financial code

Every formula needs, before it can inform a recommendation (README §15):

- golden vectors with independently-reasoned expected values;
- property-based invariants that must hold for every input;
- boundary cases: zero, negative, maximum, exact half-way rounding points;
- deterministic seeding, so a failure is reproducible from the seed alone.

Invariants worth asserting: principal repaid equals original principal within declared
rounding; a higher interest rate cannot reduce total interest, all else equal; a
prepayment cannot increase remaining principal; allocation conserves the total;
simulation never mutates canonical state.

## Authorization code

Negative tests are the point. Happy path alone proves nothing (README §9):

```
owner allowed · other workspace denied · membership without grant denied
revoked member denied · support masked-only · admin scoped
service principal least privilege
```

## Never

Do not weaken an assertion, lower a threshold or skip a test to make CI green. If a
test is genuinely wrong, fix the test and say why in the PR.
